# FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS DOCUMENT (FRD)

## Care to Cure Patient Retention & Follow-up Management System

**Organization:** Care to Cure
**Country:** Philippines
**Document Type:** Functional Requirements Document
**Version:** 1.0
**Status:** Draft
**Prepared By:** Business Analyst

---

# 1. Document Purpose

The purpose of this Functional Requirements Document (FRD) is to define the functional requirements for the proposed **Care to Cure Patient Retention & Follow-up Management System**.

The system will support the management and tracking of the patient journey from appointment booking through consultation, procedures, follow-ups, feedback, and retention analysis.

The system is intended to provide Care to Cure with better visibility into:

* Appointment attendance
* No-shows
* Cancellations
* Rescheduling
* Procedure completion
* Follow-up compliance
* Patient feedback
* Patient drop-offs
* Doctor performance
* Department performance
* Patient retention

**Billing, payment processing, insurance claims, and financial management are outside the scope of this system.**

---

# 2. Project Objectives

The system shall enable Care to Cure to:

1. Centralize patient appointment information.
2. Track appointment status throughout its lifecycle.
3. Capture cancellation and no-show reasons.
4. Track rescheduled appointments.
5. Track consultation outcomes.
6. Track recommended procedures.
7. Track procedure completion and non-completion.
8. Track required follow-up appointments.
9. Monitor follow-up attendance.
10. Capture patient feedback.
11. Calculate patient retention and drop-off metrics.
12. Provide doctor and department performance metrics.
13. Provide management dashboards.
14. Identify recurring patient drop-off patterns.

---

# 3. Scope

## 3.1 In Scope

The system will include the following modules:

* Patient Management
* Department Management
* Doctor Management
* Appointment Management
* Appointment Confirmation & Reminder Tracking
* No-show and Cancellation Management
* Rescheduling
* Consultation Tracking
* Procedure Management
* Follow-up Management
* Patient Feedback
* Retention & Drop-off Analytics
* Doctor Performance Analytics
* Department Performance Analytics
* Management Dashboard

---

## 3.2 Out of Scope

The following functions are excluded:

* Billing
* Invoicing
* Payment processing
* Insurance claims
* Accounts receivable
* Revenue management
* Financial reporting
* Payroll
* Pharmacy management
* Inventory management

---

# 4. User Roles

| Role                    | Description                                                    |
| ----------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Hospital Administrator  | Manages overall system configuration and access                |
| Front Desk Staff        | Manages patients, appointments, confirmations and attendance   |
| Doctor                  | Manages consultation, procedure recommendations and follow-ups |
| Department Head         | Reviews department-level performance                           |
| Patient Experience Team | Reviews feedback and patient experience                        |
| Hospital Management     | Reviews dashboards and KPIs                                    |
| IT Administrator        | Manages technical configuration and users                      |
| Business Analyst        | Defines requirements and analyzes business processes           |
| BI/Analytics User       | Creates and reviews analytical reports                         |

---

# 5. Functional Requirements

## 5.1 Patient Management

### FR-001 — Create Patient Record

The system shall allow authorized users to create a patient record.

The patient record shall contain relevant information such as:

* Patient ID
* Patient name
* Date of birth
* Gender
* Contact information
* Preferred communication method
* Registration date

The system shall generate a unique Patient ID.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-002 — Search Patient

The system shall allow authorized users to search for patients using:

* Patient ID
* Patient name
* Contact information

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-003 — View Patient Journey

The system shall allow authorized users to view a patient's relevant journey information in a consolidated view.

The view should include:

**Appointments → Consultations → Procedures → Follow-ups → Feedback**

**Priority:** High

---

# 6. Department Management

### FR-004 — Maintain Departments

The system shall maintain hospital departments.

Initial departments include:

* General Medicine
* Cardiology
* Orthopedics
* Pediatrics
* Obstetrics & Gynecology
* Dermatology
* ENT
* Ophthalmology
* Neurology
* Gastroenterology
* Pulmonology
* Dental
* Physiotherapy
* General Surgery
* Emergency

Emergency encounters shall be separately identified for analytics because emergency care does not follow the same appointment behavior as scheduled outpatient visits.

**Priority:** High

---

# 7. Doctor Management

### FR-005 — Create Doctor Profile

The system shall allow authorized users to create and maintain doctor profiles.

Information may include:

* Doctor ID
* Doctor name
* Department
* Specialty
* Availability status

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-006 — Assign Doctor to Appointment

The system shall allow a doctor to be assigned to an appointment.

**Priority:** High

---

# 8. Appointment Management

### FR-007 — Create Appointment

The system shall allow authorized users to create an appointment.

Required information shall include:

* Appointment ID
* Patient ID
* Doctor
* Department
* Appointment date
* Appointment time
* Appointment type
* Booking channel
* Appointment status

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-008 — Appointment Status

The system shall support the following appointment statuses:

* Requested
* Scheduled
* Confirmed
* Rescheduled
* Cancelled
* No-show
* Completed

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-009 — Update Appointment

Authorized users shall be able to update appointment information before the appointment occurs.

The system shall maintain relevant changes to appointment status.

**Priority:** High

---

# 9. Appointment Confirmation

### FR-010 — Record Appointment Confirmation

The system shall record whether the patient has confirmed the appointment.

Possible values:

* Confirmed
* Pending
* Unable to Confirm

The system shall store the confirmation date/time where applicable.

**Priority:** High

---

# 10. Appointment Reminder

### FR-011 — Generate Appointment Reminder

The system shall support appointment reminder functionality before the scheduled appointment.

Reminder information shall include:

* Patient
* Appointment
* Reminder date/time
* Communication channel
* Reminder status

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-012 — Track Reminder Status

The system shall track whether the reminder was:

* Sent
* Delivered
* Failed
* Responded to, where supported

**Priority:** Medium

---

# 11. Cancellation Management

### FR-013 — Cancel Appointment

Authorized users shall be able to cancel an appointment.

The system shall require or provide a cancellation reason.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-014 — Capture Cancellation Reason

The system shall support standardized cancellation reasons, including:

* Forgot appointment
* Transportation problem
* Scheduling conflict
* Personal reason
* Patient feeling better
* Doctor unavailable
* Long waiting time
* Communication issue
* Other

**Priority:** High

---

# 12. No-show Management

### FR-015 — Record No-show

Authorized users shall be able to mark an appointment as a no-show.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-016 — Capture No-show Reason

The system shall allow staff to record the reason for a no-show where available.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-017 — No-show Follow-up

The system should identify no-show appointments requiring follow-up or rescheduling.

**Priority:** Medium

---

# 13. Rescheduling

### FR-018 — Reschedule Appointment

Authorized users shall be able to reschedule an appointment.

The system shall create or update the new appointment while maintaining a relationship with the original appointment.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-019 — Track Rescheduling History

The system shall maintain the history of appointment rescheduling.

The history should include:

* Original appointment
* New appointment
* Rescheduling date
* Reason, where available

**Priority:** High

---

# 14. Consultation Management

### FR-020 — Record Consultation

The doctor shall be able to record that the consultation has been completed.

The consultation shall be linked to:

* Patient
* Appointment
* Doctor
* Department

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-021 — Record Consultation Outcome

The system shall support consultation outcomes such as:

* No further action
* Follow-up required
* Procedure recommended
* Referral required

**Priority:** High

---

# 15. Procedure Management

### FR-022 — Record Procedure Recommendation

The doctor or authorized user shall be able to record a recommended procedure.

The system shall capture:

* Procedure ID
* Patient ID
* Doctor
* Department
* Procedure type
* Recommendation date
* Recommended date
* Patient decision

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-023 — Record Patient Procedure Decision

The system shall support:

* Accepted
* Declined
* Deferred
* Needs more information

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-024 — Schedule Procedure

Authorized users shall be able to schedule an accepted procedure.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-025 — Procedure Status

The system shall support:

* Recommended
* Scheduled
* Confirmed
* Completed
* Cancelled
* No-show
* Declined
* Deferred

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-026 — Capture Procedure Non-completion Reason

If a procedure is not completed, the system shall allow the user to record the reason.

Possible reasons include:

* Patient declined
* Patient postponed
* Scheduling conflict
* Transportation issue
* Communication issue
* Patient unavailable
* Other

**Priority:** High

---

# 16. Follow-up Management

### FR-027 — Record Follow-up Requirement

The system shall allow the doctor to indicate whether follow-up is required.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-028 — Create Follow-up Appointment

Authorized users shall be able to create a follow-up appointment.

The follow-up shall be linked to the relevant patient and previous care event.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-029 — Track Follow-up Status

The system shall support:

* Required
* Scheduled
* Confirmed
* Completed
* Cancelled
* No-show
* Rescheduled

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-030 — Track Follow-up Attendance

The system shall record whether the patient attended the required follow-up.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-031 — Capture Follow-up Non-attendance Reason

The system shall allow users to record cancellation/no-show reasons for follow-up appointments.

**Priority:** Medium

---

# 17. Patient Feedback

### FR-032 — Capture Patient Feedback

The system shall allow patient feedback to be recorded.

Feedback fields may include:

* Overall satisfaction
* Doctor rating
* Staff rating
* Waiting-time experience
* Appointment experience
* Communication experience
* Comments
* Complaint/issue category

**Priority:** Medium

---

### FR-033 — Link Feedback to Patient Journey

Where possible, feedback shall be linked to the relevant:

* Appointment
* Procedure
* Follow-up

**Priority:** Medium

---

# 18. Retention & Drop-off Management

### FR-034 — Identify Appointment Drop-offs

The system shall identify patients who:

* Cancel appointments
* Miss appointments
* Repeatedly reschedule

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-035 — Identify Procedure Drop-offs

The system shall identify patients who receive procedure recommendations but do not complete them.

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-036 — Identify Follow-up Drop-offs

The system shall identify patients who require follow-up but:

* Do not schedule it
* Cancel it
* Miss it
* Do not return

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-037 — Identify Repeat Drop-off Patients

The system should identify patients with repeated drop-off events.

Example:

**No-show → Rescheduled → No-show → Follow-up missed**

**Priority:** High

---

# 19. KPI Calculation

### FR-038 — Attendance Rate

The system shall calculate:

**Attendance Rate = Completed Appointments ÷ Scheduled Appointments × 100**

---

### FR-039 — No-show Rate

The system shall calculate:

**No-show Rate = No-show Appointments ÷ Scheduled Appointments × 100**

---

### FR-040 — Cancellation Rate

The system shall calculate:

**Cancellation Rate = Cancelled Appointments ÷ Scheduled Appointments × 100**

---

### FR-041 — Procedure Completion Rate

The system shall calculate procedure completion using an agreed denominator, such as recommended or scheduled procedures.

**Procedure Completion Rate = Completed Procedures ÷ Applicable Procedure Population × 100**

The final denominator must be agreed with business stakeholders.

---

### FR-042 — Follow-up Compliance

The system shall calculate:

**Follow-up Compliance = Completed Follow-ups ÷ Required Follow-ups × 100**

---

### FR-043 — Patient Retention Rate

The system shall calculate patient retention based on an agreed measurement window.

Example:

**Returning Patients within defined window ÷ Eligible Patients × 100**

The business must confirm whether the standard window will be **90 days, 180 days, or another agreed period.**

**Priority:** High

---

# 20. Doctor Performance

### FR-044 — Doctor Performance Metrics

The system shall provide doctor-level metrics including:

* Appointment volume
* Attendance rate
* No-show rate
* Cancellation rate
* Patient satisfaction
* Procedure completion
* Follow-up compliance

**Priority:** Medium

---

# 21. Department Performance

### FR-045 — Department Performance Metrics

The system shall provide department-level metrics including:

* Appointment volume
* Attendance rate
* No-show rate
* Cancellation rate
* Procedure completion
* Follow-up compliance
* Patient satisfaction
* Retention rate

**Priority:** High

---

# 22. Dashboard & Reporting

### FR-046 — Management Dashboard

The system shall provide a management dashboard containing key patient journey KPIs.

The dashboard should display:

* Total appointments
* Attendance rate
* No-show rate
* Cancellation rate
* Procedure completion rate
* Follow-up compliance
* Retention rate
* Patient satisfaction

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-047 — Dashboard Filters

Users shall be able to filter dashboard information by:

* Date
* Department
* Doctor
* Appointment type
* Patient segment
* Appointment status

**Priority:** High

---

### FR-048 — Drop-off Dashboard

The dashboard shall provide visibility into drop-offs at:

1. Appointment attendance
2. Procedure completion
3. Follow-up attendance
4. Future/return care

**Priority:** High

---

# 23. Reporting Requirements

The system should support the following reports.

### Report 1 — Appointment Report

Fields:

* Appointment ID
* Patient ID
* Department
* Doctor
* Appointment date
* Appointment type
* Status
* Cancellation/no-show reason

---

### Report 2 — Procedure Report

Fields:

* Patient ID
* Doctor
* Department
* Procedure
* Recommendation date
* Scheduled date
* Status
* Non-completion reason

---

### Report 3 — Follow-up Report

Fields:

* Patient ID
* Doctor
* Department
* Follow-up type
* Required date
* Scheduled date
* Attendance status
* Reason for non-attendance

---

### Report 4 — Patient Retention Report

Fields:

* Patient ID
* First visit date
* Last visit date
* Number of visits
* No-show count
* Cancellation count
* Procedure status
* Follow-up status
* Retention status

---

# 24. Business Rules

### BR-001

Every appointment must be associated with a valid patient.

### BR-002

Every appointment must have a doctor and department unless the appointment type/business process explicitly allows otherwise.

### BR-003

An appointment cannot be marked as completed unless attendance has been recorded.

### BR-004

A cancelled appointment should have a cancellation reason where available.

### BR-005

A no-show appointment should have a no-show reason where available.

### BR-006

A rescheduled appointment must maintain traceability to the original appointment.

### BR-007

A procedure recommendation must be associated with a consultation or relevant care event.

### BR-008

A completed procedure must have a valid procedure record.

### BR-009

A follow-up marked as completed must have an associated follow-up appointment/event.

### BR-010

Emergency encounters must be separately identified from scheduled outpatient appointments.

### BR-011

Retention calculations must use an approved business definition and measurement window.

### BR-012

Doctor and department performance metrics must use standardized KPI definitions.

---

# 25. Functional Workflow

## Appointment Workflow

**Request**

↓

**Scheduled**

↓

**Confirmed**

↓

**Reminder**

↓

**Attended?**

### Yes

**Consultation**

### No

**Cancelled / No-show**

↓

**Reason Captured**

↓

**Reschedule / Follow-up**

---

## Procedure Workflow

**Procedure Recommended**

↓

**Patient Decision**

↓

**Accepted?**

### Yes

**Scheduled**

↓

**Confirmed**

↓

**Attended?**

↓

**Completed**

### No

**Declined / Deferred**

or

**Cancelled / No-show**

---

## Follow-up Workflow

**Follow-up Required**

↓

**Scheduled**

↓

**Confirmed**

↓

**Reminder**

↓

**Attended?**

### Yes

**Follow-up Completed**

### No

**Cancelled / No-show**

↓

**Reschedule / Patient Drop-off**

---

# 26. Non-Functional Requirements

Although this document primarily focuses on functional requirements, the following non-functional requirements should be considered.

## NFR-001 — Security

Only authorized users shall be able to access patient information.

## NFR-002 — Role-based Access

Users shall only access functions appropriate to their role.

## NFR-003 — Auditability

Important changes to patient, appointment, procedure, and follow-up information should be auditable.

## NFR-004 — Performance

Common system operations should respond within an acceptable time defined during technical design.

## NFR-005 — Availability

The system should be available during agreed hospital operating hours and required support periods.

## NFR-006 — Data Privacy

The system must comply with applicable healthcare data protection and privacy requirements.

For portfolio development and demonstration, only **synthetic/de-identified patient data** should be used.

---

# 27. Data Entities

The initial logical data model should contain the following entities:

1. Patient
2. Doctor
3. Department
4. Appointment
5. Appointment Reminder
6. Consultation
7. Procedure
8. Follow-up
9. Feedback
10. Cancellation/No-show Reason
11. User
12. Audit Log

Relationships include:

**Patient → Appointments**

**Doctor → Appointments**

**Department → Doctors**

**Appointment → Consultation**

**Consultation → Procedure**

**Patient → Procedures**

**Procedure → Follow-up**

**Patient → Follow-ups**

**Appointment → Feedback**

**Procedure → Feedback**

**Follow-up → Feedback**

---

